IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp1-nouns`
IMPORT `cp1-months-helpers`
IMPORT `cp1-div-b-contributory-salary-and-wages`
IMPORT `cp1-div-b-self-employed-earnings`
IMPORT `cp1-div-b-maximum-earnings-and-exemption`

-- Tests of cp1-div-b-maximum-earnings-and-exemption.l4: sections 16 to 20.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the text before the file was run. Ages go through section 2(2): the age
-- is deemed reached on the first day of the month after the birthday, except in paragraphs 17(c), 17.1(c), 19(c) and 19(d), where
-- the actual birthday governs. The Year's figures are the illustrative 2024-style figures (68,500; 73,200; 3,500) used in the
-- other test files, not readings of the Wage Measure, which the text does not contain.

§ `Tests -- section 18: the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings`

#ASSERT `s 18(1)(a) — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for 1987` EQUALS 25_900
#ASSERT `s 18(1)(b) — the amount calculated for 1988` 500 400 EQUALS JUST 32_375   -- 25,900 x 500/400
#ASSERT `s 18(1)(b) — the amount calculated for 1988` 390 400 EQUALS JUST 25_252.5   -- 25,900 x 390/400
#ASSERT `s 18(1)(b) — the amount calculated for 1988` 500 0 EQUALS NOTHING   -- a nil denominator
#ASSERT `s 18(1)(c) — the amount calculated for 1989 and each subsequent year` 32_375 450 500 EQUALS JUST 29_137.5   -- 32,375 x 450/500
#ASSERT `s 18(1)(c) — the amount calculated for 1989 and each subsequent year` 32_375 550 500 EQUALS JUST 35_612.5   -- 32,375 x 550/500
#ASSERT `s 18(1)(c) — the amount calculated for 1989 and each subsequent year` 32_375 550 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(1) — the amount calculated for a year` 1986 25_900 500 400 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(1) — the amount calculated for a year` 1987 0 500 400 EQUALS JUST 25_900
#ASSERT `s 18(1) — the amount calculated for a year` 1988 0 500 400 EQUALS JUST 32_375   -- paragraph (b): the preceding-year figure is the 1987 amount in (a)
#ASSERT `s 18(1) — the amount calculated for a year` 1989 32_375 450 500 EQUALS JUST 29_137.5   -- paragraph (c)
#ASSERT `s 18(1) — the amount calculated for a year` 1989 32_375 450 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(2) — the amount rounded down to a multiple of one hundred dollars` 32_375 EQUALS 32_300
#ASSERT `s 18(2) — the amount rounded down to a multiple of one hundred dollars` 32_300 EQUALS 32_300   -- already a multiple of 100: unchanged
#ASSERT `s 18(2) — the amount rounded down to a multiple of one hundred dollars` 35_612.5 EQUALS 35_600
#ASSERT `s 18(2) — the amount rounded down to a multiple of one hundred dollars` 35_699.99 EQUALS 35_600
#ASSERT `s 18(3) — the amount the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings is increased to` 29_137.5 32_300 EQUALS JUST 32_300   -- less than the preceding year: increased to it
#ASSERT `s 18(3) — the amount the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings is increased to` 32_300 32_300 EQUALS NOTHING   -- equal to the preceding year: not less, not increased
#ASSERT `s 18(3) — the amount the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings is increased to` 35_612.5 32_300 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 1986 25_900 0 EQUALS NOTHING   -- the text gives nothing before 1987
#ASSERT `s 18 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 1987 0 0 EQUALS JUST 25_900
#ASSERT `s 18 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 1988 32_375 25_900 EQUALS JUST 32_300   -- rounded down
#ASSERT `s 18 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 1988 25_252.5 25_900 EQUALS JUST 25_900   -- raised to the preceding year (subsection (3)), not rounded
#ASSERT `s 18 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 1988 26_000 25_900 EQUALS JUST 26_000   -- a multiple of 100 already
#ASSERT `s 18 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 1989 35_612.5 32_300 EQUALS JUST 35_600
#ASSERT `s 18 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 1989 29_137.5 32_300 EQUALS JUST 32_300
#ASSERT `s 18 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 1990 32_350 32_300 EQUALS JUST 32_300   -- 32,350 is not less than 32,300; rounded down to 32,300
#ASSERT `s 18(5) — the Wage Measure for a month` TRUE 800.5 790 EQUALS 800.5   -- the Industrial Aggregate, while it is published
#ASSERT `s 18(5) — the Wage Measure for a month` FALSE 800.5 790 EQUALS 790   -- the measure prescribed by regulation once it ceases to be published
`a revision published on 10 January 2020` MEANS `cp1 Published figure` WITH `date the figure is published` IS (YMD 2020 1 10), `the published figure` IS 800.1
`a revision published on 1 March 2020` MEANS `cp1 Published figure` WITH `date the figure is published` IS (YMD 2020 3 1), `the published figure` IS 801.2
`a revision published on 1 May 2020` MEANS `cp1 Published figure` WITH `date the figure is published` IS (YMD 2020 5 1), `the published figure` IS 799.99
`a second revision published on 1 March 2020` MEANS `cp1 Published figure` WITH `date the figure is published` IS (YMD 2020 3 1), `the published figure` IS 801.5
#ASSERT `s 18(6) — the revision of the Wage Measure published most recently prior to the calculation` (LIST `a revision published on 10 January 2020`, `a revision published on 1 March 2020`, `a revision published on 1 May 2020`) (YMD 2020 4 1) EQUALS JUST 801.2   -- the 1 March revision is the latest before 1 April
#ASSERT `s 18(6) — the revision of the Wage Measure published most recently prior to the calculation` (LIST `a revision published on 10 January 2020`, `a revision published on 1 March 2020`, `a revision published on 1 May 2020`) (YMD 2020 6 1) EQUALS JUST 799.99
#ASSERT `s 18(6) — the revision of the Wage Measure published most recently prior to the calculation` (LIST `a revision published on 10 January 2020`, `a revision published on 1 March 2020`) (YMD 2020 3 1) EQUALS JUST 800.1   -- a revision published on the day of the calculation is not "prior to" it
#ASSERT `s 18(6) — the revision of the Wage Measure published most recently prior to the calculation` (LIST `a revision published on 10 January 2020`) (YMD 2020 1 10) EQUALS NOTHING   -- none published before
#ASSERT `s 18(6) — the revision of the Wage Measure published most recently prior to the calculation` EMPTY (YMD 2020 1 10) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(6) — the revision of the Wage Measure published most recently prior to the calculation` (LIST `a revision published on 1 March 2020`, `a second revision published on 1 March 2020`) (YMD 2020 4 1) EQUALS JUST 801.5   -- two on one day: the later in the list
#ASSERT `s 18(7) — the average to be used for the twelve month period` 500 506 500.5 EQUALS 500.5   -- a difference of 6 is more than 1% of 500 (5): the Minister's adjusted average
#ASSERT `s 18(7) — the average to be used for the twelve month period` 500 505 500.5 EQUALS 505   -- a difference of exactly 5 is not more than 1%: the new basis
#ASSERT `s 18(7) — the average to be used for the twelve month period` 500 494 500.5 EQUALS 500.5   -- a fall of 6 is also a difference of more than 1%
#ASSERT `s 18(7) — the average to be used for the twelve month period` 500 495 500.5 EQUALS 495   -- a fall of exactly 5
#ASSERT `s 18(8) — subsection (7) has ceased to apply` 24 EQUALS TRUE   -- twenty-four consecutive months
#ASSERT `s 18(8) — subsection (7) has ceased to apply` 23 EQUALS FALSE

§ `Tests -- section 18.1 and section 20`
#ASSERT `s 18.1 — the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 2024 68_500 EQUALS JUST 73_200   -- 1.07 x 68,500 = 73,295 ; the next multiple of 100 below is 73,200
#ASSERT `s 18.1 — the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 2025 71_300 EQUALS JUST 81_200   -- 1.14 x 71,300 = 81,282
#ASSERT `s 18.1 — the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 2025 70_000 EQUALS JUST 79_800   -- 1.14 x 70,000 = 79,800, already a multiple of 100
#ASSERT `s 18.1 — the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 2023 66_600 EQUALS NOTHING   -- the section begins with 2024
#ASSERT `s 18.1 — the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 2030 80_000 EQUALS JUST 91_200   -- 1.14 x 80,000
#ASSERT `s 18.1(1) — the amount calculated for the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` 2024 68_500 EQUALS JUST 73_295
#ASSERT `s 18.1(2) — the amount rounded down to a multiple of one hundred dollars` 73_295 EQUALS 73_200
#ASSERT `s 20 — the Year's Basic Exemption` 2024 68_500 EQUALS JUST 3_500   -- after 1997 : 3,500
#ASSERT `s 20 — the Year's Basic Exemption` 1998 36_900 EQUALS JUST 3_500
#ASSERT `s 20 — the Year's Basic Exemption` 1997 35_800 EQUALS JUST 3_500   -- 10% of 35,800 is 3,580 : the highest multiple of 100 not above it is 3,500
#ASSERT `s 20 — the Year's Basic Exemption` 1997 36_900 EQUALS JUST 3_600   -- 10% is 3,690
#ASSERT `s 20 — the Year's Basic Exemption` 1997 36_000 EQUALS JUST 3_600   -- 10% is exactly 3,600 : "less than or equal to"
#ASSERT `s 20 — the Year's Basic Exemption` 1987 25_900 EQUALS JUST 2_500   -- 10% is 2,590
#ASSERT `s 20 — the Year's Basic Exemption` 1986 25_900 EQUALS NOTHING   -- the text gives no Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings before 1987

